WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.467
The extent of

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.001
damage is

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.535
being increasingly is becoming

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.437
rather increasingly clear in Haiti

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.873
after a weekend of torrential downpours

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.942
and widespread flooding.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.110
At least 42

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.111
people are dead,

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.445
dozens more injured

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.748
and thousands of homes destroyed.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.383
Dramatic scenes like this

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.118
are taking place across the country.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.520
And as residents try to outrun

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.521
the rising waters,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.155
often

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.923
with little more than the clothes

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.225
on their backs.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.192
And now we're learning

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.827
at least four people were killed

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.929
and 36 others injured.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.831
Following a 4.9 earthquake

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.733
that struck Haiti earlier today.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.834
The Caribbean island nation

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.636
is no stranger to hardship.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.771
It's already struggling

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.272
with devastating

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.775
gang violence and political instability

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:42.942
while teetering on

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.511
the brink of economic collapse.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:44.878
The U.N.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.047
says even before this weekend's rain,

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.448
nearly half of Haiti's

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.916
population was in need

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.885
of humanitarian assistance.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.254
Gary Pierre is the founder and editor

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.588
of The Haitian Times.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.524
He joins us live now.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.124
So, Gary,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.126
thank you so much for being with us.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.495
I wish we could talk about Haiti

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.831
in a much more positive context.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.132
But here's the thing

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.200
just in terms of the situation

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.034
on the ground.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.602
Gangs approximately control

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.271
about 80% of Port au Prince.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.606
Obviously, you have vigilante

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.408
vigilantes that have sort of

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.744
now gone up against the gangs

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.012
and are attacking the gangs.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:19.412
And essentially

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.947
taking the law into their own hands.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.416
You also have flooding in various parts

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:23.950
of the country.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.852
On top of that, an earthquake

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.887
that struck this morning.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:28.655
How is Haiti

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.924
coping with these Back-To-Back

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.425
humanitarian disasters?

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.061
Thanks for having me, Zain.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:35.862
And I must say,

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.564
my heart goes out to my fellow

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.965
Haitians in Haiti.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.333
Who have been suffering so much.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.167
But, you know,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.270
this is a result of chronic bad

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.205
governance

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.474
that that's been decades in the making.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.908
And we've seen the results.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.276
Right now,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:53.113
there is no functioning government for

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.647
for what it's worth.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.484
People are left on their own to survive,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.285
to defend for themselves.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:01:59.853
The state,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.055
the police can no longer provide that.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.123
And on top of that,

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.591
we have these natural disasters.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.959
Well, we know that Haiti's

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.926
and the Caribbean,

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.395
when it comes to major in July or August,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.764
these are hurricane seasons, months.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.466
And so

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.635
there's very little that the governments

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.769
pass and

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.073
have done to mitigate the disasters

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.641
once they come.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.409
And so we need

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.778
a governance restore in Haiti

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.681
and so that the state can provide

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.984
the people with the help when

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:31.951
they need it.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:33.820
So what are you hearing in

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.888
terms of what's happening in the ground?

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.488
I mean, obviously,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.323
this these particular floods

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.360
have largely spared Port-Au-Prince.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.928
Not entirely, but largely.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.764
But there are still thousands of people.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.966
13,000 people displaced

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.034
as a result of these floods.

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.002
What are you hearing from

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.736
the ground in terms of

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.138
what is the greatest need at this point?

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:55.508
Food, drinking water, I imagine shelter,

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.509
especially for those people

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.912
who no longer have a place to live.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.581
The biggest need is shelter right now,

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.949
because you have to remember

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.884
that on top of these displaced people,

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.319
there were already displaced

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.820
people fleeing gang violence.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.421
In the country

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.156
as and the city, as you mentioned.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:10.723
And so right

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.825
now, people need water and shelter.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.495
And we have reporters on the ground

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.398
working, reporting as we speak

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.601
on the conditions and what the needs are.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.437
So in terms of

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.040
humanitarian groups and aid agencies,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.441
what are they up against?

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.009
Because, yes, on the one

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.612
hand, you're navigating

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.414
humanitarian crises

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.615
just in terms of the flooding,

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.849
which a lot of these aid

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.484
agencies are used to.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.752
But the environment is

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.020
particularly unique.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.388
You've got gangs

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.390
controlling several parts of Port

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:44.824
au Prince.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.025
And then on top of that,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:46.993
you have

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.094
these vigilantes

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.229
who, as I mentioned,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.830
have taken the law into their own hands

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.565
and who are now

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:56.102
attacking and murdering suspected.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.204
This is key suspected gang members.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:58.838
They don't even know

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.206
whether they're gang members for sure.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.241
But if they suspect

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.842
they're a gang member,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.977
they could end up dead

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.112
at the hands of these vigilante groups.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:08.081
So what are the unique challenges

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.382
for aid agencies

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.783
operating in this kind of environment?

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.652
Well,

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.553
first of all,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.655
many of these aid organizations

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.223
stop their work in Haiti,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.926
most notably Doctors Without Borders,

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.160
because the situation

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.662
been so dangerous for them,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.197
because they were operating

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.065
and gang controlled territory.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.368
And other aid organizations

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.769
left for the most part

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.772
or have had their work

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.274
curtailed significantly.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.809
So right now, it's unclear

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.044
what the government

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.380
is doing to alleviate the problem because

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.148
the biggest.

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.183
The other challenges, the gangs situation

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.752
because while you

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.220
you do have the vigilante

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.588
the back alley movement

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:51.090
that's also dangerous because it could

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.925
you know, go into lawlessness

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.794
the likes we haven't seen in Haiti

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:55.561
where

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.230
suspected people

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.932
use that movement to settle scores.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:00.700
And then you have

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.135
another mess in our hands.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.069
And so I think

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.439
the police need to regain control.

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:09.442
And also now to help facilitate

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.244
the humanitarian aid

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.313
that's desperately needed right now

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.614
with this earthquake

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:15.548
in the south

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.617
and the rain across the country.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:18.951
I mean, I remember

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.719
seeing images of

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.753
of police officers

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.722
protesting in the streets

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.090
because they just

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.258
didn't know what to do

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.360
in terms of controlling these gangs.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.062
Acting Prime Minister Ariel Sharon,

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.897
we did make an urgent plea

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.298
to the international community.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.733
He wanted outside

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.268
international intervention,

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:37.170
possibly led by Canada

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.539
or the United States or the U.N.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.007
to come and assist in terms

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.442
of containing

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:44.077
the gang violence in the country

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.044
where are we on that?

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.312
Because a lot of these countries

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.681
were reluctant to lead any such group.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:49.182
Where does.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:49.849
Where are we on that

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:50.950
and where does that leave Haiti?

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.220
Well, where we are, there is

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.756
CARICOM is trying to broker some kind of

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.393
movement, a deal

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:03.696
with the army and the opposition.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.398
The primary opposition group

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.066
is the Montana Accord.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.301
And so,

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.001
you know,

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.370
CARICOM is not equipped

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.337
to deal with Haiti

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.772
and the international community.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:13.306
The U.N.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.108
has had a shaky

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:17.610
past, and its interventions in the U.S.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.044
right now

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.445
is just is not interested

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.347
and going back to Haiti.

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.116
And so while

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.517
the international community

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.819
trying to figure out how to help,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.155
I think what needs what they can do

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.757
concretely is to help

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.358
the police regain control.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.994
Right now, the police department in Haiti

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.963
is under arms embargo

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.798
while arms are flowing

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.099
into the gangs hands.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.801
And so this is unfair.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:44.170
And they need material.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.240
They need all kinds of weapons

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.674
to fight these gangs

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:51.310
so that the country can have a chance

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:52.812
to stabilize itself

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:54.781
and get back on the way

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.883
to functioning democracy,

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.017
which, you know, is

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.686
and there is no elected official

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:01.587
in Haiti.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:02.588
So right now,

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.590
Haiti's a democracy in name only.

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.559
It is not a practicing

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.461
or functioning democracy.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.163
And a lot of people have issues

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.031
with the acting prime minister,

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.933
Oriol Honoré,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.468
I wish we had time to talk about that

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.135
a little bit longer,

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.804
but I am out of time.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.237
Gary,

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:19.672
thank you so much for being with us.

